---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { facts, operator } from '../lib/site';

const subject = encodeURIComponent('Delete my AlgoMinutes account');
---
<Base
  title="Delete your account"
  description="How to delete your AlgoMinutes account and everything in it: in the app, or by asking us."
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Delete your AlgoMinutes account</h1>
    <p>
      Deleting your account permanently deletes everything in it. It can't be undone.
    </p>

    <h2 id="in-app">In the app (fastest)</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Open AlgoMinutes and go to <strong>Settings</strong>.</li>
      <li>Choose <strong>Delete my account</strong>.</li>
      <li>Type <strong>DELETE</strong> to confirm.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Your account is deleted straight away. If you signed in with Apple, AlgoMinutes also revokes its access to your Apple ID.</p>

    <h2 id="by-email">If you can't use the app</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href={`mailto:${operator.privacy}?subject=${subject}`}>{operator.privacy}</a> with the subject
      "Delete my AlgoMinutes account", from the email address you sign in with. If you can, include your
      <strong>User ID</strong> from Settings. We'll confirm the account is yours, delete it within 30 days (usually much
      sooner), and reply when it's done.
    </p>

    <h2 id="what">What's deleted</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Every recording, transcript, summary, action item, decision and chapter.</li>
      <li>Your search index.</li>
      <li>Your account, settings, product events, support messages and device push tokens.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Everything is deleted from our live systems at once, and from our backups within {facts.backupWindowDays} days.
      Server logs that mention your account's ID expire within {facts.logRetentionDays} days.
      We keep a record that the account was deleted (its IDs, with no content) for 30 days, so it can't be recreated
      by mistake, and payment records for as long as tax law requires once subscriptions are sold.
    </p>
    <p>To delete a single note instead, open it in the app and choose <strong>Delete</strong>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
